{{Quote|We'll rely on each other up there, like we always do. And as long as we do that, I'll go up against anything in the galaxy and like our chances.|Garven Dreis to the rest of Red Squadron before the Battle of Yavin|<ref name="Duty Roster">{{StoryCite|story=Duty Roster|book=From a Certain Point of View}}</ref>}}
'''Garven''' "'''Dave'''" '''Dreis''', dubbed "'''Old Man'''" by the other [[pilot]]s at [[Great Temple|Base One]], was a [[Gender|male]] [[human]] and [[ace]] [[Rebel pilot|pilot]] from [[Virujansi]] who served as a [[commander]] in the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] during the [[Galactic Civil War]]. During the war, Dreis flew a [[Red One (T-65B X-wing starfighter)|T-65B X-wing starfighter]] as [[Red Leader|leader]] of [[Red Squadron (Rebel Alliance)|Red Squadron]] in the Rebellion's support of [[Rogue One]]'s incursion at the [[Battle of Scarif]], and in the Rebellion's attack on the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|first Death Star]] in the [[Battle of Yavin]]. During the latter battle, he was [[Death|killed]] by [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]].

==Biography==
===Life on Virujansi===
Garven Dreis was [[Reproduction|born]] on the [[planet]] [[Virujansi]] prior to the [[Clone Wars]]. After making a name for himself during the [[Cloning|Clone]] Wars,<ref name="Duty Roster" /> Dreis joined the [[Planetary defense forces|planetary defense force]] known as the [[Virujansi Rarified Air Cavalry]] on his [[homeworld]]. After the [[Proclamation of the New Order|formation]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], Virujansi experienced a political transformation when an Imperial [[governor]] displaced the ruling [[Virujansi council]]. This resulted in the forced disbanding of local military forces loyal to the ruling council. Dreis's [[commanding officer]], [[Antoc Merrick]], rejected an offer extended to [[pilot]]s of the Rarified Air Cavalry to join the [[Imperial Navy]], seeing it as hollow. Seeing that the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance's]] [[starfighter]] [[squadron]]s demonstrated greater unit cohesion and piloting ability than those of the Empire, Dreis and Merrick opted for early retirement, left Virujansi, and sought membership with the Rebel Alliance.<ref name="Rogue One Visual Guide" />

===Serving the Rebellion===
Sometime around the [[Battle of Atollon]] in [[2 BBY]], Dreis joined the Rebel Alliance,<ref name="Timelines" /> eventually attaining the [[Military rank|rank]] of [[Commander]].<ref name="Rebel Files">''[[Star Wars: The Rebel Files]]''</ref> He was given command of [[Red Squadron (Rebel Alliance)|Red Squadron]],<ref name="Episode IV" /> and as [[Red Leader]], Dreis flew a mix of starfighters, that ranged from [[Aggressive ReConnaissance-170 starfighter]]<ref name="FFG ARC-170">{{FFGXW2|set=Rebel Alliance Conversion Kit|cardname=Garven Dreis}}</ref> to the [[Red One (T-65B X-wing starfighter)|T-65B X-wing starfighter]].<ref name="Episode IV" />

Dreis was posted at the Alliance's base on Dantooine, but was later transferred to Yavin 4's [[Great Temple]] sometime before the Battle of Yavin.<ref name="SWCT">{{SWCT|set=Base Series 1|cardname=Garven Dreis - Rebel Alliance}}</ref> At some point prior to [[1 BBY]], Dreis was scheduled for Shift Cycle 1 of an [[T-65B X-wing starfighter|X-wing]] flight patrol mission along with [[Major]] [[Ralo Surrel]] ([[Red Eleven]]). Their mission was to route from [[Yavin Prime|Yavin]] to [[Gordian Reach|Gordian]] Trace Relays, perform a flyby of surrounding space, then after verifying visual and sensor all clear, perform close uplink of passive relay recordings.<ref name="Rebel Files" />

====Battle of Scarif====
{{Quote|Stick close, Red Five! Where are you going?|Dreis calls out to Pedrin Gaul during the Battle of Scarif|<ref name="Rogue One">''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref>}}
[[File:Garven_Dreis_Scarif.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Garven Dreis during the Battle of Scarif]]
In 1 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|BBY]],<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> Dreis led [[Color|Red]] Squadron as part of the [[Alliance Military|Rebel Alliance's forces]] supporting the [[Rogue One]] team, which had [[Battle of Scarif|attacked]] the planet [[Scarif]] in an attempt to obtain [[Death Star plans|schematics]] for the Empire's [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]]. As part of [[Admiral]] [[Raddus]]' plans during the early phase of the engagement, Red Squadron and [[Gold Squadron (Rebel Alliance)|Gold Squadron]], a [[BTL-A4 Y-wing assault starfighter/bomber|Y-wing]] [[bomber]] group, were assigned to protect the Rebel [[capital ship]]s, with Blue Squadron being ordered to the surface of Scarif to protect their infantry. Fighters under Dreis' command also engaged the large [[TIE/ln space superiority starfighter|TIE fighter]] detachment guarding the Scarif [[Shield Gate]].<ref name="Rogue One" />

X-wings under Dreis' command, including [[Red Eight]] and [[Red Twelve (Rebel Alliance)|Red Twelve]], attempted to penetrate the shield proper of the Scarif gate with repeated [[proton torpedo]] bombing runs in conjunction with Gold Squadron's attacks on the aperture itself. Despite their continued bombardment throughout the engagement, the Rebel [[Starship|ships]] were unable to break through the powerful Imperial shield.<ref name="Rogue One" />

As a result of these runs, the TIE fighter complement directly intercepted the Rebel fighter and bomber forces, including Dreis' squadron. Dreis chided<ref name="Rogue One" /> [[Pedrin Gaul]], a [[cadet]] pressed into active service with the squadron under the [[callsign]] [[Red Five]],<ref name="Rogue One Visual Guide" /> for splitting off from the main group. Despite Dreis' instruction for Gaul to return, the latter was shot down, along with several other Red Squadron members. Dreis survived Scarif, and his [[Rebel pilot|pilots]] were a direct cause for the Rebel Alliance victory that resulted from this attack.<ref name="Rogue One" />

====Battle of Yavin====
{{Quote|Skywalker, you sure you can handle this ship?<br />"Sir, Luke is the best bush pilot in the Outer Rim Territories."<br />"You'll do all right."<br />"Thank you, sir. I'll try.|Garven speaks with Biggs Darklighter and Luke Skywalker before the Battle of Yavin|<ref name="Episode IV" />}}
Shortly after the costly victory over Scarif, Dreis and his remaining pilots were summoned to a briefing at Base One by [[General]] [[Jan Dodonna]]. [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] of [[Alderaan]], a Rebel sympathizer who had taken possession of the plans for the monolithic [[Death Star]] [[battle station]] as a result of the battle over Scarif, had briefly [[Secret mission to Tatooine|fallen]] into Imperial custody, while the plans had been secreted within a [[droid]], [[R2-D2]], which eventually found its way to [[Luke Skywalker]], a [[Tatooine]] [[moisture farmer]]. Motivated by a message from Organa which guided him to [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], a hidden [[Jedi]], Skywalker had hired a [[Corellian]] [[smuggler]], [[Han Solo]], and, through a series of events, [[Rescue of Princess Leia|rescued]] Organa from [[Prison|imprisonment]] and returned the plans to her, although Kenobi was killed shortly before the group escaped the Death Star. Their means of escape was Solo's [[freighter]], the ''[[Millennium Falcon]]'', which had, unbeknownst to Organa and her compatriots, been tagged with an Imperial [[Homing beacon|tracking device]]. The Death Star and its ruthless commander, [[Grand Moff]] [[Wilhuff Tarkin]], had been guided to the Rebel stronghold on [[Yavin 4]], and had arrived [[Yavin system|in-system]] shortly before the briefing.<ref name="Episode IV" />

Dreis, along with most of those assembled, were skeptical that the handful of fighters remaining could have any effect on the Death Star. Dodonna explained, however, that there was a key flaw in the designs of the station: a [[thermal exhaust port]], only two [[meter]]s wide. A proton torpedo fired down this shaft would impact the main [[reactor]], causing critical failure and, ultimately, the destruction of the Death Star.<ref name="Episode IV" />

Returning to the hangar, Dreis met with Skywalker, who had volunteered to join the squadron and bolster their numbers. Dreis was initially skeptical of the young man's piloting skills; however, [[Biggs Darklighter]], a childhood friend of Skywalker and already a pilot under Dreis' command, personally vouched for his piloting skills, boasting that Luke was the best bush pilot in the entire [[Outer Rim Territories]]. Dreis accepted Skywalker and assigned him to the position of Red Five,<ref name="Episode IV" /> left vacant after cadet Pedrin Gaul's death over Scarif.<ref name="Rogue One" />

The squadron, scrambled alongside [[Captain]] [[Jon Vander]]'s [[BTL Y-wing starfighter|Y-wings]] once again, rose from Yavin 4's [[jungle]]s and flew to the Death Star, along the way confirming readiness and checking in. Arcing toward the [[Meridian trench|trench]] and their target, the squadrons quickly began suffering losses to the [[XX-9 heavy turbolaser battery|turbolaser batteries]] and deflection towers across the surface of the [[moon]]-sized battle station. Dreis' [[X-wing starfighter|X-wings]] initially served as cover while the bombers of Gold Squadron peeled off in groups of three to attempt the trench run; however, as [[Black Squadron (Galactic Empire)|squadrons]] of TIE fighters poured from the Death Star's [[hangar]] bays to engage the rebel ships, these early runs were annihilated to the last man.<ref name="Episode IV" />

[[File:Garven_Dreis_last_moments.png|thumb|right|250px|Dreis' last moments at the Battle of Yavin]]
[[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]], a [[Dark Lord of the Sith]], emerged from the station in a [[Darth Vader's TIE Advanced|TIE Advanced x1]] to aid in the Imperial defense. He was responsible for the deaths of several of Dreis' subordinates in Red Squadron as well as three separate members of Gold Squadron, including Captain Vander, in dogfights. Despite this danger, Dreis, [[Theron Nett]], and [[Puck Naeco]] attempted the trench run.<ref name="Episode IV" />

Although Vader shot down both of Dreis' [[Wingmate|wingmen]], Dreis reached the end of the trench and fired two proton torpedoes at the exhaust port. Initially believing he was successful, Dreis disappointingly realized that his torpedoes missed their mark, only impacting the surface. While arcing out of the trench to recover from his failed attack, Dreis was targeted by Vader. Skywalker, seeing the Imperial fighters, told Dreis that he would come to his aid for another trench run; the squadron leader dissuaded him from this, as his starboard [[engine]] had been damaged, and ordered him to make a run on the trench himself. He then led Vader as far from the trench as he could before he was finally shot down by the Dark Lord. Letting out one final defiant yell, Dreis' X-wing spiraled into the surface of the Death Star, and he was killed on impact.<ref name="Episode IV" />

===Legacy===
{{Quote|To Dreis, Branon, Porkins, Rue, Dinnes, Naytaan, Nett, Surrel, Naeco&hellip;|Skywalker, honoring Dreis and Red Squadron's actions|<ref name="Star Wars 45">[[Star Wars (2015) 45|''Star Wars'' (2015) 45]]</ref>}}
In [[1 ABY]],<ref name="Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of [[Star Wars (2015) 45|''Star Wars'' (2015) 45]] to [[1 ABY]].</ref> Skywalker and fellow rebels [[Han Solo]], [[Wedge Antilles]], [[Zev Senesca]], [[Derek Klivian]], and [[Chewbacca]] raised a [[Toast (ritual)|toast]] at [[Mess Hall IV]] in the [[Mako-Ta Space Docks]] to honor the deceased members of Red Squadron, including Dreis.<ref name="Star Wars 45" />

==Equipment==
[[File:Garven_Dreis_Helmet.jpg|thumb|right|200px|Garven Dreis' flight helmet]]
As a pilot of the rebellion, Garven Dreis wore an orange [[flight suit]] and [[flight helmet]] with red and yellow markings, while piloting a T-65B X-wing starfighter known as ''Red One'',<ref name="Desert Son">{{StoryCite|story=Desert Son|book=From a Certain Point of View}}</ref> manufactured by [[Incom Corporation]].<ref name="USW" /> His [[astromech droid]] was [[R5-K6]].<ref name="Episode IV" />

==Behind the scenes==
Garven Dreis was portrayed in [[1977]]'s [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']] by British actor [[Drewe Henley]] (whose last name was incorrectly spelled "Hemley" in the credits, including those of the [[The Star Wars Trilogy Special Edition|Special Edition]]). A pre-battle scene in which Dreis discusses Luke's piloting ability and meeting Luke’s father when he was young with Luke and Biggs was cut from the original release, but partially restored in 1997 for the Special Edition.

Henley passed away on February 14, 2016. His role in ''A New Hope'' was his final acting role on film; shortly after the movie was released, he was diagnosed with manic depression and retired. Henley posthumously reprised the role in [[2016]]'s ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]'' through the use of archival footage.

On page 46 of the 2016 reference book ''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]'', Dreis' last name was misspelled "Dries."<ref name="Rogue One Visual Guide" />

Dreis' helmet used in the film was carried by a pilot on [[Hoth]] in [[Star Wars: Episode V The Empire Strikes Back|''The Empire Strikes Back'']] (named [[Nichos Panib]] in [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]]) and on ''[[Home One]]'' in [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Return of the Jedi'']].<ref name="Costumes">''[[Star Wars Costumes: The Original Trilogy]]''</ref> The film prop was reused for the character [[Ina Rece]] in Legends video game [[Star Wars: Rebel Assault II: The Hidden Empire|''Rebel Assault II: The Hidden Empire'']].<ref name="RAII video">{{LucasArts|url=products/rebel2/reb_vid.htm|text=''Rebel Assault II'' - Live Action Video}}</ref>

